.TH MD_PROCESS 3 "2026-10-16" "libmorsedec 0.3.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
md_process \- feed mono floating-point audio samples
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <morsedec.h>

int md_process(morsedec_decoder_t *decoder, const float *samples,
    size_t count);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Feed mono floating-point audio samples.
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I decoder
Decoder handle. Calls using this handle must be serialized, including queries.
.TP
.I samples
Input array, or NULL only when count is zero. Native C values; the library
does not decode byte order.
.TP
.I count
Number of mono scalar samples, not bytes.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns MORSEDEC_SUCCESS (1) on success, or MORSEDEC_FAILURE (0) and sets
errno on failure. Do not inspect errno after success.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
NULL decoder, NULL input with nonzero count, wrong handle type,
external-spectrum mode already selected, or input after md_flush(). Reset
before switching from spectrum input or starting a new stream after flush.
.SH REMARKS
Requires a handle from md_new(). Float and s16 sample calls may be interleaved
on an audio handle without reset.
.PP
Float values are normalized to [-1,1]. Finite values outside that range are
clamped; NaN and infinite values become zero.
.PP
Input storage is borrowed only for the duration of the call. Complete hops are
processed immediately; partial hops are retained. Chunk boundaries do not
change the result. No heap allocation, blocking I/O, or callbacks occur during
processing. Read each channel's bounded message snapshot after every
processing call. A successful zero-count call selects sample-input mode even
though it consumes no samples.
.SH THREAD SAFETY
Serialize all calls that access the same handle, including getters. Different
handles may process concurrently after construction. These functions are not
specified as async-signal-safe.
.SH VERSION
This md_ entry point is available since libmorsedec 0.2.0.
Version 0.3.0 uses the float API and shared-library ABI 2.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmorsedec (3),
.BR md_new (3),
.BR md_process_s16 (3),
.BR md_flush (3),
.BR md_get_characters (3)
